    "summary": "Councillor Ian Stutely was first elected for Town Close ward on 4 May 2018. The council's record shows them leaving on 2 May 2024 — its own reason is “Did not win re-election” — and returning on 1 May 2025. They have represented Mancroft ward since then. The council records their party as Labour from 8 May 2018 to 28 November 2023, Independent Norwich Group from 29 November 2023 to 2 May 2024 and The Green Party since 1 May 2025. They are the Deputy Leader and Cabinet member for planning and regulatory. They sit on 3 of the council's committees and panels: Cabinet, Council and Twinning committee. The council's committee system records them at 31 of the 33 meetings they were expected at in the 12 months to 8 September 2026. They missed 2, and the council records apologies for all 2. Their register of interests is published as a scan, so we cannot show what is on it; the form itself is linked.",
